------------------------------------------------------------------------
ROOT-CAUSE OF THE RED STEPS (all pre-existing, all out of allowed scope)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
The TeslaSync app target was already un-buildable on this checkout BEFORE this
surface was added. None of the failures below are in StaggerItem; StaggerItem only
ever emits the same harmless self-import warning every sibling test file emits
("file 'StaggerItem.Tests.swift' is part of module 'TeslaSync'; ignoring import").

1) `*.Tests.swift` import XCTest inside the APP target (systemic, 170 sibling
   surfaces). project.yml compiles TeslaSync/feature-views (and now shared-surfaces)
   into the app targets, including their `*.Tests.swift`. Those files
   `import XCTest`, which the app target cannot resolve:
     feature-views/AIRestorePanel.Tests.swift:18:8: error: unable to resolve
       module dependency: 'XCTest'
   This is the first hard error the iOS `build test` hits (IOS_EXIT=65). It is
   identical for all 170 sibling `.Tests.swift`; StaggerItem.Tests.swift follows the
   exact same house pattern, so any systemic fix (route `*.Tests.swift` to the test
   targets / exclude from app targets) fixes it uniformly. Fixing it here would
   require editing project.yml's app-target source rules repo-wide (and would still
   not produce a green build because of #2) — out of this prompt's allowed scope.

2) Duplicate / ambiguous types across sibling surfaces (latent behind #1). Forcing
   ENABLE_TESTING_SEARCH_PATHS=YES to get past #1 reveals pre-existing duplicate
   type definitions shared between feature-views and dashboard-widgets, e.g.:
     dashboard-widgets/VehicleHeroWidget.Content.swift:18:21: error:
       'VehicleHeroProjection' is ambiguous for type lookup in this context
   distinct ambiguous types observed: VehicleHeroProjection, VehicleHeroModel,
   VehicleHeroConnection, VehicleHeroSource, InMemoryVehicleHeroSource,
   VehicleHeroTelemetry, VehicleHeroLoadStatus, VehicleHeroUpdate,
   DashboardWidgetSize (27 compile failures). These require renaming duplicated
   symbols in sibling surfaces — out of this prompt's allowed scope, and unrelated
   to StaggerItem (whose public types were verified collision-free).

3) macOS additionally fails before compilation on code-signing (no Apple
   development certificate on this runner):
     error: "TeslaSync-macOS" has entitlements that require signing with a
       development certificate. (target 'TeslaSync-macOS')
   This is an environment/signing limitation, not a source issue.

4) whole-tree swiftformat/swiftlint reds are single pre-existing sibling files,
   NOT shared-surfaces:
     FORMAT_EXIT=1 -> feature-views/ActionBuilder.Previews.swift:48:1
                      (blankLinesBetweenScopes)
     LINT_EXIT=2  -> dashboard-widgets/LifetimeStatsWidget.Adapter.swift:141:19
                      Function Body Length (78 > 50)
   shared-surfaces contributes 0 format and 0 lint findings.

